SUMMARY:🌆🚶‍♂️ SUMMER EVENING WALK DOWN YONGE STREET & BEAVERTA
 ILS BY THE WATER 🍁🍩
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n🌆
 🚶‍♂️ SUMMER EVENING WALK DOWN YONGE STREET & BEAVERTAILS BY THE W
 ATER 🍁🍩\n\nToronto Lights\, City Energy & A Sweet Treat by the Lake\
 nThere is something special about Toronto on a summer evening.\nThe city i
 s alive. Patios are full. Street performers are out.\n\nThe energy feels c
 ompletely different once the sun starts to go down.\n\nJoin us for a relax
 ed social walk down one of the most famous streets in Canada as we make ou
 r way south along Yonge Street toward Toronto's beautiful waterfront.\n\nA
 long the way we'll enjoy the sights\, sounds\, and people-watching that ma
 ke downtown Toronto so unique. From historic buildings and busy intersecti
 ons to hidden corners of the city\, there's always something interesting h
 appening on Yonge Street.\nThis is not a historical tour.\n\nIt's a social
  walk focused on conversation\, meeting new people\, and enjoying a summer
  evening together.\n\nAnd of course...\n\nWe'll finish with one of Canada'
 s greatest inventions: BeaverTails. 🍁😄\nAfter grabbing our treats\, 
 we'll head down to the waterfront where we'll spend 30–40 minutes relaxi
 ng by the lake\, enjoying the views\, and getting to know each other.\n\n
 📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://chat.whatsa
 pp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe
 'll begin on Yonge Street and make our way south through the heart of down
 town Toronto.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n🏙️ Walk through the city core\
 n📸 Stop for photos and interesting sights\n😊 Meet new people and enj
 oy conversation\n🍁 Grab BeaverTails near the waterfront\n🌊 Relax by 
 Lake Ontario for 30–40 minutes\n🌇 Enjoy the evening skyline and water
 front atmosphere\n\nThe total experience is approximately 2 hours dependin
 g on the pace of the group.\nYou're welcome to leave at any time.\n\n***\n
 \n☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis event will happen in typical summe
 r weather conditions.\nThat means sunshine\, clouds\, heat\, humidity\, or
  light rain.\n\nThe only reason we would cancel is for severe weather or t
 hunderstorms.\nPlease dress comfortably and bring water if it's a warm eve
 ning.\nThis is a social walk\, not a race.\n\nWe'll keep a comfortable pac
 e that allows people to chat and enjoy the city.\n\n***\n\n🧢 Meetup Det
 ails\n📍 Meetup Location: Outside the subway station\n🫎 I'll be weari
 ng my Moose Hat\n⏰ Meetup Time: 6:30 PM\nI will only wait 5 minutes.\nEa
 rly is on time.\nOn time is late.\n\nWe will leave promptly and won't be a
 ble to spend time tracking people down.\n\n🏁 End Point: Toronto Waterfr
 ont\n\n***\n\n🎟️ Meetup Fee: $5 cash in person or e-transfer to\n📧
  **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n\nThis
  fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events l
 ike this. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n🎒 What to 
 Bring\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Light sweater (opt
 ional for later in the evening)\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n🍁 Mon
 ey for BeaverTails\n\n***\n\n🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis group is open t
 o anyone who wants to be social and make friends — whether single or not
 .\n\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture o
 utings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\n\nThere's always something happenin
 g.\n\n***\n\nREMEMBER: You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're
  unsure about your schedule.\nAnd as always\, sometimes plans shift and ev
 ents may need to be cancelled — please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\
 n👤 Organizer: Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 
 [torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotma
 il.com)\n\nCome for the walk. Stay for the waterfront.\n\nLeave with stick
 y fingers\, a full stomach\, and a few new friends. 🌆🍁✨
